      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>In your name] Oh Merci(ful). The one who is grateful to him for his endeavors, Judah the teacher 'Amm\u0101n\u012b.</li>\n<li>My ] letter to the patron and august lord the h(onor-able), g(reat) (and) h(oly) master and teacher, Elijah the judge,</li>\n<li>&hellip; prince of ] judges, may God preserve him and make his end better than his beginning;</li>\n<li>&hellip; may there be more like ] him in Israel, Amen selah. Amen Ne\u1e63ah\u0323 selah. Now, then; may</li>\n<li>you know what is in our hearts on account of &hellip;&hellip;&hellip; and the</li>\n<li>&hellip;. Virtu]ous, the important and noble lady, the pure and righteous one, may her soul</li>\n<li>&hellip; ] Eden with the righteous and pious. Our heart has been rent.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
